# Electron / electron-vite build output
out/
*.local

# Lab generated secrets - NEVER commit private keys or certs
lab/certs/*.key
lab/certs/*.crt
lab/certs/*.pem
lab/certs/*.p12
lab/certs/*.srl
lab/certs/*.csr

# Zitadel lab - generated state and any future per-machine secrets
lab/zitadel/data/
lab/zitadel/.env
lab/zitadel/secrets/
# Auto-seed output (Zitadel PAT written by setup.sh's FirstInstance) - NEVER commit
lab/zitadel/.seed/

# Runtime env written by lab/setup.sh - per-machine fresh client_id + abs CA path. NEVER commit.
lab/.runtime-env

# Kill-switch lab - signing keypair is generated FRESH per machine by lab/setup.sh (the public
# half is env-injected via DTL_KILL_PUBLIC_KEY_PEM, not a fixed shipped fixture). Neither half is
# committed. The committed lab/kill/kill-*.json samples were signed against the original fixed dev
# key and are reference-only; they won't verify against a fresh one.
lab/kill/*.key
lab/kill/kill-signing.pub

# Kill-command active file - overwritten by lab/setup.sh (fresh signed no-op) and reset by
# lab/teardown.sh on every run. Generated, not shipped.
lab/kill/kill-command.json

# Internal design docs - milestone plans + process/reasoning docs, moved out of plans/ and docs/
# for the handoff repo. Stay ON DISK (untracked) so Claude Code's two-tier plan-gate keeps
# working - new plans are written here going forward (see CLAUDE.md). History of everything
# moved here is preserved via `git log -- plans/<file>` / `git log -- docs/<file>` even after
# `git rm --cached`.
docs/internal/

electron.vite.config.*.mjs